  "headline": "City of Pearls and Nizams",
  "short_description": "Hyderabad blends Qutb Shahi and Nizam-era monuments with a booming IT sector and world-famous biryani.",
  "about": "Founded in 1591 by the Qutb Shahi dynasty, Hyderabad later flourished under the Nizams and today is Telangana's capital and a major technology hub.\n\nLocated on the Deccan Plateau in southern Telangana, around the Hussain Sagar lake.\n\nKnown for Hyderabadi Urdu, pearl trading, Nizami architecture and its distinctive biryani.\n\nA significant centre of Deccani Islamic heritage alongside a large Hindu population.",
  "history": "Built around the Charminar as a planned city by Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah, later the seat of the wealthy Nizams of Hyderabad until independence.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Rajiv Gandhi International Airport (airport)\n- Secunderabad Junction (railway)\n- Mahatma Gandhi Bus Station (MGBS) (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Telugu, Urdu, Hindi, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to February",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Rajiv Gandhi International Airport (HYD)",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Secunderabad Junction / Hyderabad Deccan",
